CommitDate: Sun Nov 1 17:02:58 2026 +0800

    [BugFix][v0.32.0rc] Fix GLM-5.3-Flash PCP query, decode and packed KV layouts (#20513)
    
    ### What this PR does / why we need it?
    
    Backport #20512 to `releases/v0.32.0rc`: align KPool query rows, NoPE
    metadata capacity, replicated decode and packed-KV slot mapping.
    
    KPool decode remains replicated; no new PCP mode or configuration is
    introduced.
    
    The runner now calls `AscendPCPManager.bind_config()` at the existing
    config-binding point. Decode policy is resolved inside the manager
    before replication queries, without adding configuration fields.
    
    Fixes #20510. Refs #15665.
    
    ### Does this PR introduce _any_ user-facing change?
    
    Yes. Fixes GLM-5.3-Flash MRV2 PCP failures and incorrect answers in
    mixed prefill/decode batches.
    
    ### How was this patch tested?
    
    - Updated worker suites: 270 passed, 1 skipped; source and test mypy
    checks passed separately. Current-head
    [pre-commit/mypy](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm-ascend/actions/runs/41282800763/job/124777973197)
    passed. Previous-head full CPU CI passed: [vLLM
    main](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm-ascend/actions/runs/41215146112/job/124579348114)
    (14470 tests),
    [v0.32.0](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm-ascend/actions/runs/41215146112/job/124579348113)
    (14454 tests).
    - Earlier main-fix hardware validation, before this initialization
    refactor: A3 PCP8/MTP5 cold/warm checks: 32/32 eager and 32/32
    FULL_DECODE_ONLY. Same-request P control changed from HTTP 500 (20 index
    rows/24 queries) to HTTP 200. Uses existing KDA fix #20281.
    - Earlier AIME2026 validation, all 30 problems, model/output limits
    1048576/131072: colocated 29/30; real PD 28/30. Remaining answers hit
    the output limit; no engine errors. Five colocated zero-output transport
    failures were retried with identical bodies. PD verified eager P,
    target/draft graph replay on D, and successful KV READs for every
    request. These scores do not establish full accuracy equivalence to an
    unpatched baseline.
    
    - vLLM main:
    https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/commit/544f182d9f0c9bfe8bd7645525951d5e3692a542
    
    ---------
    
    Signed-off-by: Li Jiahang <216526138+lijiahang226@users.noreply.github.com>

